--
-- WHY THE SENATE WAS THIN
-- Not for want of roll calls: every one of these is already here and already carries
-- curated issue mappings. The ingest attributes a vote only to a member in
-- db/vr-member-map.json, that map is read out of the curated portrait shelf, and the
-- shelf had no photo for fifty-five sitting senators — including the chairs and ranking
-- members of Appropriations, Armed Services, Agriculture, Commerce, Energy & Natural
-- Resources, Environment & Public Works, Finance, HELP, Homeland Security, Intelligence
-- and Veterans' Affairs. A senator with no face could not be attributed a vote at all,
-- so the people who run the committees were the people whose records looked emptiest.
--
-- WHERE THE CELLS COME FROM
-- senate.gov's LIS roll-call XML — the Secretary of the Senate's own document. Each was
-- identity-verified before a cell was taken from it: congress, session, vote_number, the
-- measure the document says it is about (or its parent, or — for a nomination filed under
-- a human label — the nominee's surname AND the office they were confirmed to), the
-- document's own yea/nay/present/absent counts against the members it actually lists, an
-- LIS id on every member, and a vote_cast vocabulary we recognise. 54 rolls were checked;
-- 4 were dropped whole:
--   119/1 roll (none stored) · Vought — OMB: no roll number stored, so there is no LIS document to verify against
--   119/1 roll (none stored) · Rubio — State: no roll number stored, so there is no LIS document to verify against
--   119/1 roll (none stored) · McMahon — ED: no roll number stored, so there is no LIS document to verify against
--   119/1 roll (none stored) · Gabbard — DNI: no roll number stored, so there is no LIS document to verify against
-- A further 2 verified roll(s) are already complete and appear here not at all: every
-- member their document lists is a cell we already hold. Kept + refused + complete closes
-- on the number considered, so nothing was dropped without saying so.
--
-- IDENTITY RUNS THROUGH PUBLISHED IDENTIFIERS, NOT NAMES
-- <lis_member_id> → Bioguide (congress-legislators, current and historical) → profile
-- slug (db/vr-member-map.json). No name matching, no state-and-party inference. An LIS id
-- that does not resolve is skipped and counted, never guessed.
--
-- is_party IS RECOMPUTED, NOT INHERITED
-- Each cell's is_party is derived from the full chamber tally in the same document the
-- vote was read from — the member's own party's yea/nay split on that roll — so it
-- describes where they stood among their colleagues on that vote and nothing else. It
-- is a stored fact about the roll, not a score, and nothing in the product ranks on it.
--
-- 1 CELL(S) THIS MIGRATION REFUSES TO TOUCH
-- 2410 cells already stored on these rolls were re-read against the Senate's
-- document and agree. 1 do not:
--   119/1 roll 160: roger_marshall stored 'nay', document says 'not_voting'
-- This migration is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING throughout, so it cannot overwrite them.
-- Correcting a stored vote is a deliberate act with its own citation and belongs in its
-- own migration, not in the quiet middle of a densification pass.
--
-- Seed → member-map agreement: 2166 cached politicianId(s) re-checked against
-- db/vr-member-map.json at generation time; 0 stale, 0 unresolvable.

